  "hypothesis": "The frozen feature-matching loss spends gradients fitting a component removed by final LN. A single finite control tests whether this changes the 100-step coefficient recovery. Native predictions are invariant in exact arithmetic. This mechanism is distinct from changing the AGA assignment with null shifts.",
  "equations": "Bnew=B+lambda*ones(d)/sqrt(d)*v.T. v is the leading right singular vector of original B after removing its rank32 task right subspace. lambda is the positive solution of norm(Bnew-Bexpert)=3.999996*norm(Bexpert). Each token receives a scalar all-channel shift. LN(h+c1)=LN(h), while raw MSE splits into centered error plus squared mean error.",
  "fixed_scope": "One output-matrix control on the same parent. No A change, rank/scale search, optimizer, generated images, or training of the defense. Parameter budget remains B<=4. The standard ProDistill has the original 64 unlabeled training images per task and100 updates/block. No effect is assumed.",
  "limitations": "Mean invariance is known from Layer Normalization; this is a diagnostic component, not a new defense claim. Column-centering the output weight and bias is an explicit data-free removal. Even a standard-ProDistill benefit would not establish resilience to that cleanup, all recovery, or a sufficient core contribution.",
  "evaluation": "Freeze before images. Evaluate the full10000MNIST against the identical parent and require identical predictions and maximum logit difference<=0.0005 for this mathematical-invariance control. If passed run the fixed fullMNIST/SVHN distillation using the existing adapter and matched clean result. Report every outcome; no change to main method from this control alone.",
